{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"106531","commit":"14527caf012faf2f217b26520dcf1874e228b066","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The code changes introduce new functionality to associate API keys with user profiles and handle realms more effectively. However, there are several areas that need attention:\n- The `ApiKeyOwnerProfileIntegTests` class introduces a new test suite for verifying the association of API keys with user profiles. Ensure that all edge cases are covered, such as when users belong to different domains or when profiles are not yet activated.\n- In `ApiKeyIntegTests`, methods like `getApiKeyInfoWithProfileUid` and `getAllApiKeyInfoWithProfileUid` should be well-documented to explain their purpose and usage.\n- The changes in `TransportGetApiKeyAction` and `TransportQueryApiKeyAction` to include profile resolution are significant. Ensure that the performance impact is minimal, especially when dealing with a large number of API keys or profiles.\n- In `ProfileService`, the method `resolveProfileUidsForApiKeys` should handle cases where some subjects do not have associated profiles gracefully. Consider adding logging or metrics to track such occurrences.\n- The changes in `QueryApiKeyRequest` and related tests need to ensure that the new `withProfileUid` parameter is correctly validated and used across all scenarios.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ProfileService.java-x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ProfileService.java-6700:6718-7069:7092,7102:7144","promptId":"#7PDWW","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ProfileService.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ProfileService.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6700,"endPos":6718,"startLine":137,"startLineOffset":34,"endLine":137,"endLineOffset":52,"length":19}],"dstChanges":[{"po